    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/domeinarchitect-domeinen-bedrijfsvoering-en-onderwijs-1512/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Domeinarchitect Domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs",
      "description": "Domeinarchitect Domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Domeinarchitect Domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs Apply now Domeinarchitect Domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs This vacancy is only available in Dutch Binnen de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) zoeken we naar een enterprisearchitect, die in staat is om een visie op architectuur en informatievoorziening te formuleren en op strategisch niveau te adviseren. Een verantwoordelijke baan waarbij je je inzet voor de Domeinen Onderwijs en Organisatiesystemen. Centrum voor Informatie Technologie 0.8 - 1 FTE €6.934 - €7.573 Share this vacancy Domeinarchitect Domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/domeinarchitect-domeinen-bedrijfsvoering-en-onderwijs-1512/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Als informatie-architect ben je verantwoordelijk voor het opstellen en uitdragen van een toekomstgerichte informatiestrategie binnen de domeinen Bedrijfsvoering en Onderwijs. Je ontwikkelt de informatie- en applicatiearchitectuur binnen deze domeinen en bent in staat om van de grond af een solide architectuur op te zetten. Je vertrekt vanuit de businessinformatiebehoeften van de organisatie en bestaande architectuurkaders. Hierbij houd je rekening met lokale, landelijke en internationale ontwikkelingen, zodat de architectuur altijd actueel en toekomstbestendig blijft. Je zorgt voor de afstemming van de informatiearchitectuur binnen de domeinen met de overkoepelende enterprise-architectuur en draagt, als lid van het architectengilde, bij aan het opstellen en handhaven van standaarden en principes. Daarnaast stem je de informatie-architectuur af op de strategie en de zakelijke doelen van de organisatie. Je staat voortdurend in contact met interne stakeholders op strategisch en tactisch niveau, en met leveranciers om de architectuur up-to-date te houden. Je kent de koers van de organisatie en bent op de hoogte van relevante wet- en regelgeving. Je maakt deel uit van het advies en architectuur Team Business Information en Consultancy (BIC) van het domein Bedrijfsvoering en een nog te bepalen team in het domein Onderwijs. Je werkt in deze twee domeinen onder de Domeinmanager Bedrijfsvoering en de Domeinmanager Onderwijs. Centrum voor Informatie Technologie €6.934 - €7.573 Wie ben jij? Jij bent overtuigend en vol zelfvertrouwen. Je communiceert makkelijk op alle niveaus en weet op natuurlijke wijze verbinding te maken en mensen voor je te winnen. Ontwikkelingen binnen je vakgebied volg je op de voet. Jouw visie en kennis van architectuurmethoden, standaarden en tools deel je met collega’s bij faculteiten en diensten. Je herkent jezelf in de kernwaarden binnen het CIT: respect, collegialiteit, samen, fun, openheid en commitment. Verder ben je in het bezit van: Een voor de functie relevante hbo- of wo-opleiding. Aantoonbare ervaring in het werkveld van informatievoorziening, met name werkzaamheden gerelateerd aan architectuur, informatiebeveiliging en gegevensuitwisseling’ Affiniteit en bekendheid met: TOGAF, Scaled Agile Framework (SAFe), HORA, ArchiMate, BPMN en Agile scrum/kanban. Je kent de geldende wet- en regelgeving, zoals onder andere de AVG, de AI-act, en de Cyberbeveiligingswet. Je bent analytisch sterk en weet complexe problemen te vertalen naar oplossingsrichtingen op een abstract niveau. Je bent een natuurlijke netwerker die in complexe organisaties snel nieuwe contacten legt en initiatieven opstart. Je hebt goede communicatieve vaardigheden waarmee je op strategisch en tactisch niveau de techniek en de business bij elkaar weet te brengen. Je hebt een groeimindset: je blijft je kennis en vaardigheden ontwikkelen. Je durft vragen te stellen en staat open voor nieuwe inzichten en uitdagingen. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    6.934\n                                          (salary scale 12.6)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    7.573                    (salary scale 12)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Aanvang jaarcontract, bij bewezen geschiktheid hoort contract voor onbepaalde tijd tot de mogelijkheid. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Center for Information Technology (CIT) at the University of Groningen supports and facilitates academic research and university education through high-quality data and IT solutions, advice, and training. Our mission is Teaching and research: supported by innovative and reliable IT services . With over 300 staff members, we manage the University’s IT infrastructure and supporting processes. To effectively support the strategic objectives of the University on a daily basis, we work in a customer-oriented way with self-organizing teams in the areas of Teaching, Research, Organizational Systems, Basic Workplaces, and Infrastructure. Our core values are excellence, expertise, and customer orientation. If you would like to learn more about the Center for Information Technology, visit rug.nl/cit . Het CIT treedt op als enabler en innovator in onderwijs en onderzoek. Met personeel en faciliteiten van het hoogste niveau en nauwe samenwerking met de klanten binnen de RUG organisatie ontwikkelt het CIT bestaande en nieuwe diensten. Het CIT zet daarmee de kracht van de universitaire organisatie in om te innoveren en zo de kwaliteit van de universiteit in brede zin te verbeteren. Op deze manier draagt het CIT bij aan een aantrekkelijke universiteit voor studenten en onderzoekers. string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: Cv, motivatiebrief Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Jeroen Schreurs Product- and businessmanager J.P.A.Schreurs@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Susan van Veenen Afdelingshoofd s.w.e.van.veenen@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-in-systems-and-control-theory-for-energy-based-learning-2430/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD Position in Systems and Control Theory for Energy-based Learning",
      "description": "PhD Position in Systems and Control Theory for Energy-based Learning - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD Position in Systems and Control Theory for Energy-based Learning Apply now PhD PhD Position in Systems and Control Theory for Energy-based Learning This vacancy is only available in English Are you excited about developing new mathematical foundations for energy-efficient computing? Do you want to contribute to cutting-edge research at the intersection of systems and control theory, optimization, circuit theory, and neuromorphic computing? The University of Groningen is seeking a highly motivated PhD candidate to work on a fundamental research project on systems and control theory for learning in neuromorphic circuits. Neuromorphic computing is an analog, brain-inspired computing paradigm with the potential to drastically reduce energy consumption while enabling faster inference than conventional digital architectures. A major challenge, however, is the development and analysis of dedicated algorithms for training analog circuits directly from data. In this PhD project, you will develop a novel system-theoretic framework for learning in analog circuits and dissipative networks. We will view learning as a feedback interconnection of continuous-time (circuit) dynamics and an optimization algorithm. The key idea is to develop algorithms that minimise cost functions inspired by notions of energy, leading to highly efficient, local learning rules. Faculty of Science and Engineering 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD Position in Systems and Control Theory for Energy-based Learning Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-in-systems-and-control-theory-for-energy-based-learning-2430/?lang=en What are you going to do? As a PhD candidate, you will develop mathematical theory for learning in nonlinear and dynamic circuits. Building on preliminary results for resistive circuits, you will study circuits containing memristive and capacitive elements, as well as more general dissipative networks. The project combines systems and control theory, circuit theory, optimization, and machine learning, with the ultimate goal of advancing the mathematical foundations of physics-based learning. Your responsibilities include: Developing a system-theoretic framework that models learning as the feedback interconnection between continuous-time circuit dynamics and optimization algorithms. Designing novel energy-based learning algorithms for training analog circuits directly from input-output data. Developing fully decentralised learning rules that rely on local circuit information and are suitable for large-scale systems. Establishing rigorous theoretical guarantees for convergence and scalability of the proposed learning algorithms. Extending the theory from analog circuits to more general dissipative networks. Testing and validating the developed methods. Publishing research findings in leading international journals and conferences and presenting your work at scientific meetings. Contributing to teaching activities and supervising Bachelor’s and Master’s students where appropriate. Faculty of Science and Engineering €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for an enthusiastic researcher who enjoys solving challenging problems and working in an international research environment. You should have: A Master’s degree in Systems and Control, (Applied) Mathematics, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related field. A strong mathematical background and an interest in conducting theoretical research. Excellent English communication skills, both written and spoken. Strong analytical abilities, creativity, persistence, and the ability to collaborate effectively. Familiarity with circuit theory, networked systems, machine learning, or neuromorphic computing is considered an advantage, but is not required. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. We offer you, following the Collective Labour Agreement for Dutch Universities:\n\na salary of € 3,204 gross per month in the first year, up to a maximum of € 4,051 gross per month in the fourth and final year for a full-time working week\na holiday allowance of 8% gross annual income and an 8.3% year-end bonus\nTeaching: employed PhD candidates are expected to spend 10% of their working hours on teaching\na full-time position (1.0 FTE). The successful candidate will first be offered a temporary position of one year with the option of renewal for another three years. Prolongation of the contract is contingent on sufficient progress in the first year to indicate that a successful completion of the PhD thesis within the next three years is to be expected. A PhD training programme is part of the agreement and the successful candidate will be enrolled in the Graduate School of Science and Engineering. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The successful candidate will join the Bernoulli Institute for Mathematics, Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence within the Faculty of Science and Engineering at the University of Groningen. The research will be carried out in the Systems, Control and Optimization Group. Our group is part of the Jan C. Willems Center for Systems and Control that unites the different control groups in Groningen. This is a leading center (ranked first in the EU (fourth in Europe) according to the 2024 Shanghai Ranking). The successful candidate will benefit from connections within the center, as well as regular seminars, joint group meetings, and interaction with other PhD students and postdocs in a lively and supportive environment. The PhD project is embedded within the European Research Council (ERC) Starting Grant project “Energy-based learning of complex dynamical systems” (E-BLOCS), led by Dr. Henk van Waarde. The PhD student will actively work together with the other members of the project, and also has many opportunities for international collaboration, research visits, and interdisciplinary training. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: ● Motivation letter (1-2 pages) ● Curriculum Vitae ● Academic transcripts (BSc and MSc) ● Contact details of two academic references ● Copy of MSc thesis (or a representative publication, if available) Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Henk van Waarde Assistant Professor H.J.van.Waarde@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Henk van Waarde Assistant Professor H.J.van.Waarde@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-in-soft-matter-modeling-for-mechanobiology-2425/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD Position in Soft-Matter Modeling for Mechanobiology",
      "description": "PhD Position in Soft-Matter Modeling for Mechanobiology - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD Position in Soft-Matter Modeling for Mechanobiology Apply now PhD PhD Position in Soft-Matter Modeling for Mechanobiology This vacancy is only available in English A 4-year PhD position is available at the interface of biophysical modeling, soft matter and cell mechanobiology at the Groningen Research Institute of Pharmacy, within the Faculty of Science and Engineering at the University of Groningen. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 16 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD Position in Soft-Matter Modeling for Mechanobiology Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-in-soft-matter-modeling-for-mechanobiology-2425/?lang=en What are you going to do? The project addresses a central question in mechanobiology: how do cells sense, encode and respond to mechanical cues? You will develop a quantitative and predictive framework that links the generation and transmission of mechanical forces to cell mechanics and intracellular signalling, with particular emphasis on mechanosensitive calcium signalling. The aim is to determine how the magnitude, spatial distribution and temporal dynamics of mechanical cues shape cellular responses. You will investigate an integrated cell–material system in which living cells are mechanically coupled to a stimuli-responsive soft material. Controlled external stimulation will deform the material and generate spatially and temporally defined forces at the cell–material interface. You will develop analytical and numerical models that predict material deformation, force transmission to cells and the resulting changes in cellular mechanics and signalling. The position is primarily computational, but a successful candidate will also contribute to experiments. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 16 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for a curious candidate who enjoys working at the interface of physics, engineering and biology, and who meets the following qualifications: Essential qualifications ·      M.Sc. degree in Applied Mathematics, Biophysics, Mechanical Engineering, Materials Science or related disciplines ·      A strong foundation in continuum mechanics and transport phenomena ·      Experience with numerical methods and finite-element modeling using COMSOL ·      An interest in biological systems and in connecting theoretical models with experimental observations ·      Enthusiasm, self-motivation, creativity, and team spirit ·      Excellent communication skills in English (verbal and written) Preferred qualifications ·      Experience with fluorescence or live-cell imaging ·      Hands-on experience with microfabrication and microfluidics ·      Familiarity with cell culture and biological assays What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least € 3.204 up to a maximum of € 4.051 (promovendus) gross per month for a full-time employment contract.\n232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours.\nEnd-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance.\nExtensive opportunities for personal and professional development.\nA temporary full-time (1.0 FTE) position for one year at first with the option of renewal for another three years. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will join The Groningen Research Institute of Pharmacy (GRIP), which is positioned within FSE, and is physically located within the University Medical Centre Groningen (UMCG) of the Faculty of Medical Sciences (FMS). Pharmaceutical research within GRIP is multidisciplinary and bridges clinical and biomedical sciences on the one hand, and chemistry, mathematics, engineering, and physics on the other. The interaction between the pharmaceutical sciences with these fundamental and clinical sciences offers excellent opportunities for cutting-edge research. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Statement of purpose . Please prepare a concise essay (maximum 2 pages) that describes your research interests and relevant research experiences, as well as your objectives in pursuing a PhD with our group. ·CV. ·Transcripts from your bachelor’s and master’s degree. ·Contact information of three references. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Vesna Bacheva Assistant Professor v.bacheva@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Vesna Bacheva Assistant Professor v.bacheva@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-data-science-2465/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position Data Science",
      "description": "PhD position Data Science - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position Data Science Apply now PhD PhD position Data Science This vacancy is only available in English Are you interested in using data science to understand how digital measures can capture clinically meaningful aspects of reward, motivation and impulsivity? Do you want to develop and apply innovative digital proxies and combine them with neurobiological markers to advance precision medicine across mental and metabolic health conditions? Then this PhD position in an international pioneering project may be an excellent opportunity for you. You will work in an interdisciplinary, international research project aiming to advance a transdiagnostic precision-medicine framework centred on Reward, Motivation and Impulsivity. The project brings together expertise in longitudinal research, biomarker discovery, clinical validation, data science, evidence synthesis and stakeholder engagement. A central ambition is to move beyond disease-specific approaches by identifying biological, behavioural and digital markers that can help characterise clinically meaningful processes across different health conditions. As a PhD candidate, you will contribute to this ambition by helping establish the evidence base for digital proxies, developing and applying data-driven measures, and investigating their relationships with neurobiological markers. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position Data Science Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-data-science-2465/?lang=en What are you going to do? We are looking for an ambitious and analytically minded PhD candidate to investigate digital proxies of Reward, Motivation and Impulsivity (RM&I) and their relationship with neurobiological markers and clinically relevant outcomes. Your work will be connecting systematic evidence synthesis, data science, longitudinal research and clinical validation. Your research will contribute to understanding whether and how digital measures can provide scalable and meaningful proxies for RM&I-related processes across major depressive disorder (MDD), Alzheimer’s disease (AD), and obesity (OB) . Your PhD research will have three closely connected components: Systematic review of digital proxies: You will systematically synthesise existing evidence on digital proxies relevant to RM&I, identifying the types of digital measures that have been investigated, their relationship with behavioural and clinical constructs, and their potential relevance for transdiagnostic research. Development and application of digital proxies: You will use data-science approaches to develop, characterise and/or evaluate RM&I-related digital proxies. You will subsequently apply these digital proxies to analyses conducted within the project’s longitudinal and clinical datasets, contributing to the identification of meaningful patterns across individuals and disease trajectories. Hypothesis testing with neurobiological markers: You will investigate relationships between digital proxies and neurobiological markers, testing hypotheses about the biological mechanisms underlying RM&I-related processes. Depending on the available data and the development of the research, this may involve integrating digital, behavioural, clinical and neurobiological measures. An important aspect of your work will be to examine the clinical and transdiagnostic relevance of digital proxies. You will contribute to determining whether digital measures can complement existing biomarkers and endpoints and help identify measurable features of RM&I that are relevant across different conditions. You will work closely with researchers involved in longitudinal cohort analyses, clinical studies, biomarker research and evidence synthesis. Your work will therefore sit at the intersection of data science, digital phenotyping, clinical research and neurobiology . Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for a motivated researcher with a strong interest in data science, digital proxies, biomarkers and clinical research. You have: A completed Master’s degree in a relevant field such as data science, artificial intelligence, computer science, neuroscience, psychology, biomedical sciences, medicine, epidemiology, health sciences or a related discipline. A strong interest in applying quantitative and computational approaches to biomedical or clinical research. Experience with statistical analysis and/or data science. Programming experience, preferably in R and/or Python. An interest in digital phenotyping, digital biomarkers, behavioural data or other digital measures. The ability to critically assess and synthesise scientific literature. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Good scientific writing and communication skills. The ability to work independently while contributing effectively to an interdisciplinary team; and Excellent written and spoken English. Experience with one or more of the following would be an advantage: Systematic reviews or evidence synthesis. Longitudinal or cohort data analysis. Multimodal or multi-omics data. Machine learning or other data-science methods. Digital phenotyping or development of digital biomarkers/proxies. Neuroimaging, electrophysiology or other neurobiological measures. Behavioural or cognitive measures. Reproducible research and open-science practices; and Research involving MDD, AD, obesity, RM&I or related transdiagnostic constructs. We particularly value candidates who are curious about how digital measures can be linked to underlying neurobiological processes and translated into meaningful research outcomes. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. A fulltime position for the duration of 48 months. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will be embedded in an interdisciplinary research environment at the University of Groningen and work as part of the international consortium. Your research will involve collaboration with scientists working on longitudinal and multimodal datasets, clinical studies, biomarker development, evidence synthesis and stakeholder engagement. The position provides opportunities to: Work with longitudinal, multimodal and potentially multi-omics datasets. Develop and apply data-science methods to clinically relevant research questions. Contribute to systematic evidence synthesis and evidence mapping. Investigate relationships between digital proxies and neurobiological markers. Collaborate across disciplines and international research teams. Present your work at international conferences and publish in peer-reviewed journals; and Contribute to scientific outputs and activities across the project. You will also participate in the doctoral training and professional development activities offered by the University of Groningen and the relevant graduate school. This position is conditional upon the grant agreement being signed and the associated funding becoming available. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV (incl. 2 references) Cover letter. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-eeg-and-neurobiological-markers-2464/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers",
      "description": "PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers Apply now PhD PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers This vacancy is only available in English Are you a motivated early-career researcher with a strong interest in EEG, neurobiology, and precision medicine ? Would you like to investigate how neurobiological markers related to reward, motivation, and impulsivity can contribute to a better understanding of health and disease? We are looking for an enthusiastic PhD candidate to join an international, multidisciplinary research programme investigating reward, motivation, and impulsivity across major depressive disorder, Alzheimer’s disease, and obesity . Your PhD research will combine three closely connected components: a systematic review of EEG measures, empirical EEG analyses, and hypothesis-driven research investigating relationships between EEG and other neurobiological markers . The position provides an opportunity to develop expertise in EEG methodology and quantitative analysis while contributing to a broader precision medicine approach that integrates evidence across different populations, research settings, and types of biological and clinical data. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position EEG and Neurobiological Markers Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-eeg-and-neurobiological-markers-2464/?lang=en What are you going to do? Your PhD research will connect systematic evidence synthesis with empirical EEG research and hypothesis-driven investigation of neurobiological markers. Systematic review of EEG measures A first component of your research will be a systematic review of EEG measures relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. You will: Develop and conduct a systematic review of EEG measures relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. Define and document search strategies and eligibility criteria. Screen and select relevant scientific literature. Extract and organise information on EEG measures, study characteristics, populations, outcomes, and relevant neurobiological markers. Synthesise and map the available evidence in a transparent and reproducible manner. Investigate the consistency and potential relevance of different EEG measures across populations and research settings. Identify promising EEG measures as well as important gaps in the existing evidence. Contribute to scientific publications and other outputs arising from the evidence synthesis. This work will provide an evidence-based foundation for the interpretation and selection of EEG measures used in the empirical research. EEG analyses A substantial part of your PhD will involve analysing EEG data generated through cohort and clinical research. Depending on the available datasets and specific research questions, you will: Contribute to the preparation, preprocessing, and quality control of EEG data. Develop and apply appropriate EEG analysis pipelines. Investigate EEG measures relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. Examine associations between EEG measures and behavioural, clinical, and other relevant variables. Analyse data collected across different populations and research settings. Contribute to the development of reproducible and well-documented analytical workflows. Interpret EEG findings in the context of the broader scientific framework. Communicate findings through scientific publications, presentations, and research meetings. You will progressively develop methodological independence and contribute to decisions concerning the analysis and interpretation of EEG data under the guidance of the supervisory team. Hypothesis testing with neurobiological markers A further aim of the PhD is to investigate hypothesis-driven relationships between EEG measures and other neurobiological markers . You will: Formulate and test hypotheses concerning relationships between neurobiological markers relevant to reward, motivation, and impulsivity. Investigate associations between EEG measures and other available biological, clinical, behavioural, or phenotypic measures. Examine whether neurobiological markers are associated with transdiagnostic dimensions of reward, motivation, and impulsivity or with relevant clinical outcomes. Apply appropriate statistical methods to test predefined hypotheses. Investigate whether combinations of neurobiological measures provide complementary information. Interpret findings in relation to existing evidence and the broader precision medicine framework. Contribute to understanding the potential of neurobiological markers for characterising clinically relevant profiles across different conditions. The precise analytical approaches will be developed in collaboration with the supervisory team and will depend on the available datasets and scientific questions. Integration of evidence and empirical research An important feature of the PhD is the connection between what is known from the literature and what can be learned from new data . You will therefore have the opportunity to: Use findings from the systematic review to inform empirical EEG analyses. Compare findings across different populations and research settings. Integrate EEG findings with other neurobiological, behavioural, and clinical measures. Critically evaluate the strengths and limitations of candidate biomarkers. Contribute to the identification of neurobiological measures that may have relevance across diagnostic categories. This integrated approach will allow you to develop a broad understanding of how EEG and other neurobiological measures can contribute to transdiagnostic and precision medicine research. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? We are looking for a highly motivated candidate with a strong interest in neuroscience, EEG, and quantitative research . You have: A Master’s degree in neuroscience, biomedical sciences, psychology, cognitive science, medicine, biology, behavioural science, or a related discipline. A strong interest in human neurobiology and EEG research. Experience with quantitative research and statistical analysis. Experience with scientific literature and academic research. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. The ability to work systematically and accurately with scientific literature and complex datasets. Excellent written and spoken English. The ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary research team. A strong motivation to develop as an independent researcher and complete a PhD within four years. You do not need to be an expert in all EEG methodologies. We are particularly interested in candidates who have a strong scientific and quantitative foundation, some relevant experience with EEG or neurophysiological research, and the motivation to develop further methodological expertise during the PhD. It is an advantage if you have Practical experience with EEG data collection, preprocessing, analysis, or interpretation. Familiarity with EEG-derived measures, such as event-related potentials, spectral measures, or time-frequency measures. Experience with EEG analysis software or programming environments such as MATLAB, Python, or R. Experience with statistical modelling or other quantitative analytical approaches. Experience working with clinical, cohort, or population-based datasets. Experience with multimodal or longitudinal data. Experience conducting systematic or scoping reviews. Familiarity with systematic-review methodology, literature searching, screening, and data extraction. Experience with biological or neurobiological markers. Knowledge of reward, motivation, impulsivity, or related cognitive and affective processes. Experience with open and reproducible research practices. Experience in all of these areas is not required. We value scientific curiosity, methodological foundations, analytical thinking, and the ability and motivation to learn new methods . What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. Temporary appointment for 1.0 FTE for 4 years. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . You will be based at the University of Groningen and become part of the GELIFES institute Neurobiology expertise group. You will work within an interdisciplinary research environment bringing together expertise in neuroscience, evidence synthesis, data analysis, and precision medicine. The research involves collaboration with academic and clinical researchers and other partners in an international research consortium. About the research programme The research programme aims to develop a transdiagnostic precision medicine framework for reward, motivation, and impulsivity across major depressive disorder, Alzheimer’s disease, and obesity. The programme combines cohort research, clinical studies, biomarker research, systematic evidence synthesis, and stakeholder engagement. It seeks to identify and evaluate measures that can improve the understanding and characterisation of reward, motivation, and impulsivity across different conditions. Your PhD will contribute specifically to the investigation of EEG and other neurobiological markers . By combining systematic evidence synthesis with empirical EEG analyses and hypothesis-driven research, you will contribute to understanding the potential value of neurobiological measures within a transdiagnostic precision medicine framework. This position is conditional upon the grant agreement being signed and the associated funding becoming available. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV Cover letter (incl. name of two references). Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Martien Kas Full Professor M.J.H.Kas@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/bestuurder-faculteit-science-engineering-2402/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering",
      "description": "Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering Apply now Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering This vacancy is only available in Dutch Wil jij als bestuurder impact maken op de koers en ontwikkeling van de Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE)? Weet jij ambities op het gebied van onderwijs en onderzoek te verbinden aan strategische keuzes rondom personeel, financiën, huisvesting en organisatie? Dan zoeken wij jou als bestuurder. Als lid van het faculteitsbestuur geef je samen met de decaan en vicedecaan richting aan de toekomst van FSE. Vanuit jouw brede portefeuille zorg je ervoor dat ambities worden vertaald naar een toekomstbestendige en doelmatige organisatie. Juist in een periode waarin financiële uitdagingen om scherpe keuzes vragen, krijg je de ruimte én verantwoordelijkheid om verschil te maken. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 12 oktober 2026 0.8 - 1 FTE €8.309 - €10.815 Share this vacancy Bestuurder Faculteit Science & Engineering Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/bestuurder-faculteit-science-engineering-2402/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Het faculteitsbestuur bestaat uit drie leden. Deze werken samen als een team en opereren als een collegiaal bestuur. Zij hebben ieder eigen aandachtsgebieden. De decaan fungeert als voorzitter en bewaakt het functioneren van het bestuur. Het faculteitsbestuur wordt bijgestaan door een student-assessor en ondersteund door een beleidsdirecteur en secretaris. Als bestuurder ben je verantwoordelijk voor personeel, financiën, huisvesting, beheer van de gebouwen en alle andere zaken op het gebied van de bedrijfsvoering. Samen met de decaan en de vicedecaan, met respectievelijk de portefeuilles onderzoek/algemene zaken en onderwijs, draag je de eindverantwoordelijkheid voor de facultaire beleidsontwikkeling en–uitvoering. Je draagt zorg voor de doelmatige organisatie van de faculteit en geeft leiding aan de (hoofden) van facultaire diensten. Daarnaast heb je een rol – samen met collega’s van andere faculteiten- bij de totstandkoming en uitvoering van het instellingsbeleid voor bedrijfsvoering. De functie vereist in het bijzonder dat je: • Het onderzoeks- en onderwijsbeleid vertaalt naar het beslag op alle soorten van middelen, in het bijzonder de personele en financiële middelen en de huisvesting. • Dit beleid eveneens vertaalt naar de vereiste vormen en omvang van ondersteuning aan de wetenschappelijke staf en naar een doelmatige inrichting van de facultaire organisatie. Dit alles moet worden vormgegeven in uitdagende financiële omstandigheden. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 12 oktober 2026 €8.309 - €10.815 Wie ben jij? Je bent een enthousiaste, gedreven professional: Met een academisch werk- en denkniveau en een sterk ontwikkeld strategisch denkvermogen. Met managementervaring bij een (grote) publieke instelling in het (hoger)onderwijs en affiniteit met wetenschappelijk onderwijs en onderzoek. Met ervaring met de financiële controlcyclus, bestuurlijke processen en administratieve procedures. Je bent helder en duidelijk over de procedures en toont souplesse waar nodig. Met ervaring op het gebied van talent- en organisatieontwikkeling, veranderingsprocessen, arbeidsvoorwaarden en andere HR-onderwerpen. Met een goed gevoel voor bestuurlijke verhoudingen en je bent daardoor in staat om met gezag te werken in een omgeving waarin professionele autonomie een grote rol speelt. Je kunt goed relaties leggen en onderhouden. Met een coachende stijl van leidinggeven en het vermogen tot delegeren waar dat mogelijk is. Met goede communicatieve vaardigheden, zowel in woord als in geschrift, in de Nederlandse en de Engelse taal. Die betrouwbaar is in afspraken en uitspraken. Die het prettig vindt om snel te schakelen tussen de vele bestuurlijke zaken, die goed past in de cultuur van de faculteit en die ook het organisatiebelang van de gehele RUG dient. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    8.309\n                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    10.815                    (salary scale 16)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Aanstelling zal plaatsvinden voor een periode van één jaar met uitzicht op een dienstverband voor onbepaalde tijd bij gebleken geschiktheid. De benoeming tot bestuurder is in principe voor vijf jaar met de mogelijkheid tot verlenging met vijf jaar. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . De missie van de Faculty of Science and Engineering richt zich op de drie pijlers onderzoek, onderwijs, en maatschappelijke impact, binnen een breed scala van de bèta- en techniekwetenschappen, en in samenwerking met partners binnen en buiten de Universiteit. Onze onderzoekers dragen bij aan het ontwikkelen van fundamentele kennis en aan het vinden van innovatieve oplossingen voor wereldwijde problemen waarmee de maatschappij te maken krijgt op het gebied van gezondheid, energie, digitalisering, duurzaamheid en weerbaarheid. Onze facultaire gemeenschap heeft een open, informeel karakter, met medewerkers en studenten uit de hele wereld. De faculteit is momenteel bezig met het formuleren van de strategie voor 2026-2031, aansluitend bij en voortbouwend op de strategie van de Universiteit. string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Rob Timmermans Hoogleraar R.G.E.Timmermans@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Grytsje van der Meer Beleidsmedewerker Grytsje.van.der.Meer@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-materials-development-for-electrically-driven-water-treatment-processes-2486/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes",
      "description": "PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes Apply now PhD PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes This vacancy is only available in English In the Engineering and Technology Institute Groningen (ENTEG), we are looking for a talented and motivated PhD student for the development and evaluation of advanced electrode materials and cell component development for sustainable electrochemical water purification technologies. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position on materials development for electrically-driven water treatment processes Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-materials-development-for-electrically-driven-water-treatment-processes-2486/?lang=en What are you going to do? In many industrial processes, chemicals are added to treat water, clean installations or separate substances from each other. Before the water can be reused or discharged, those excipients must be removed again. That costs a lot of energy, chemicals and money. The new project ECO (Electrically-driven, Chemical-free Operations) therefore chooses a different approach: prevent those excipients from being needed at all. The project will use electric fields and local pH changes close to electrodes to create the desired conditions in exactly the right place without adjusting the entire liquid. Within ECO, the PhD candidate will collaborate with 4 other PhD researchers from the University of Twente TU Delft, Wageningen University & Research and the University of Copenhagen. Companies such as Royal Avebe, FrieslandCampina, Nobian, Shell, ISPT, Ecolab and VNP are also involved in the consortium. With five PhD candidates, the consortium will investigate in the coming years how electrically driven process technologies can contribute to cleaner and more energy-efficient industrial processes. Responsibilities and tasks: Fabrication of materials and electrochemical cells with targeted characteristics. Characterization of materials and relevant interfaces for their role in the reaction mechanisms. Preparation of scientific articles and conference communications. Teaching activities (10% of total workload), including assistance to courses, as well as supervision of Bachelor and Master students. Contribution to the scientific and collaborative research environment in Chemical Engineering group and the ENTEG institute. A team player and open to collaborating in a consortium of other researchers and industrial partners, with regular consortium meetings. Ability to communicate their research to people with a broad, technical background. Handling the ‘uncertainty’ that the details of the project still need to be defined. Contribution to defining their own research, in concerted agreement with the consortium. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? A Master’s degree (or an equivalent university degree) in Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Chemistry, or related discipline. We are looking for a talented, motivated and enthusiastic researcher. Analytical skills, initiative and creativity are highly desired. You are a naturally curious person who is eager to learn more and has a strong interest in research. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English are a prerequisite. We prefer candidates with a good team spirit, who like to work in an internationally oriented, social environment. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. First, you will get a temporary position of one year with the option of renewal for another three years; prolongation of the contract is contingent on sufficient progress in the first year to indicate that successful completion of the PhD thesis within the contract period is to be expected. A PhD training program is part of the agreement and you will be enrolled in the Graduate School of the Faculty of Science and Engineering. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The Engineering and Technology institute Groningen (ENTEG) in which this position is embedded is the engineering science and technology institute of the University of Groningen, The Netherlands. ENTEG research is highly multidisciplinary in nature and focuses on fundamental and applied research on the development of new and innovative processes and products for a wide range of product sectors. Process driven research activities are performed in the field of chemical and biochemical systems, mechanical and electric systems and system networks. Typical product sectors include biobased products, tailored, complex materials such as advanced polymers or polymeric formulations, catalysts, mechatronic devices and software and algorithms. Design, control and modelling and analyses complement the activities. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Transcripts from your Bachelor’s and Master’s degree. Any other relevant documents (e.g., short research statement, awards, publications, language skills/certification, references). Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Vassilis Kyriakou Associate Professor v.kyriakou@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Kimberley ter Voorde - Speelman Human Resources Assistant k.m.ter.voorde-speelman@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-electrochemical-synthesis-of-ammonia-in-ceramic-membrane-reactors-2485/?lang=en": {
      "title": "PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors",
      "description": "PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors Apply now PhD PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors This vacancy is only available in English In the Engineering and Technology Institute Groningen (ENTEG), we are looking for a talented and motivated PhD student for the development and evaluation of (electro)catalysts for electrochemical ammonia synthesis from sustainable sources in ceramic electrochemical reactors. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 1 FTE €3.204 - €4.051 Share this vacancy PhD position on electrochemical synthesis of ammonia in ceramic membrane reactors Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/phd-position-on-electrochemical-synthesis-of-ammonia-in-ceramic-membrane-reactors-2485/?lang=en What are you going to do? Ammonia is not only a key-chemical for sustaining global population, but also an intriguing carbon-free energy carrier. Ammonia, however, is the most energy intensive commodity chemical, responsible for 1-2% of energy consumption and CO2 emissions worldwide. The PhD project will support the efforts for creating innovative electrochemical membrane reactors that produce sustainable ammonia at high efficiency for decentralized applications. The PhD research will be part of the 20.3 Meuros HyNITROGEN project (https://groenvermogennl.org/rd/werkpakket-5/) of the National Growthfund GroenvermogenNL. This unique consortium brings together more than 40 companies, universities and research institutes, covering the entire value chain. Responsibilities and tasks: Synthesis and characterization of electrocatalysts at intermediate and high temperatures. Fabrication of single cells with targeted characteristics. Characterization of materials and relevant interfaces for their role in the reaction mechanisms. Preparation of scientific articles and conference communications. Teaching activities (10% of total workload), including assistance to courses, as well as supervision of Bachelor and Master students. Contribution to the scientific and collaborative research environment in Chemical Engineering group and the ENTEG institute. Faculty of Science and Engineering Apply no later than: 30 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.204 - €4.051 Who are you? A Master’s degree (or an equivalent university degree) in Chemical Engineering, Materials Science, Chemistry, or related discipline. We are looking for a talented, motivated and enthusiastic researcher. Analytical skills, initiative and creativity are highly desired. You are a naturally curious person who is eager to learn more and has a strong interest in research. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English are a prerequisite. We prefer candidates with a good team spirit, who like to work in an internationally oriented, social environment. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.204\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.051                    (promovendus)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. First, you will get a temporary position of one year with the option of renewal for another three years; prolongation of the contract is contingent on sufficient progress in the first year to indicate that successful completion of the PhD thesis within the contract period is to be expected. A PhD training program is part of the agreement and you will be enrolled in the Graduate School of the Faculty of Science and Engineering. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Science and Engineering (FSE) provides teaching and research across a wide range of disciplines, from physics and biology to artificial intelligence, mechanical engineering, and pharmacy. In close collaboration with partners from industry, healthcare, and society, we contribute to the urgent challenges of our time, such as energy, sustainability, digitization, and medical technology. Our community is open and informal, with more than 7,000 students, 1,000 PhD students, and 1,400 staff members from all over the world. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Science and Engineering, visit rug.nl/fse . The Engineering and Technology institute Groningen (ENTEG) in which this position is embedded is the engineering science and technology institute of the University of Groningen, The Netherlands. ENTEG research is highly multidisciplinary in nature and focuses on fundamental and applied research on the development of new and innovative processes and products for a wide range of product sectors. Process driven research activities are performed in the field of chemical and biochemical systems, mechanical and electric systems and system networks. Typical product sectors include biobased products, tailored, complex materials such as advanced polymers or polymeric formulations, catalysts, mechatronic devices and software and algorithms. Design, control and modelling and analyses complement the activities. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Transcripts from your Bachelor’s and Master’s degree. Any other relevant documents (e.g., short research statement, awards, publications, language skills/certification, references). An interview, a scientific presentation and a writing assignment are part of the selection procedure. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Vassilis Kyriakou Associate Professor v.kyriakou@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Kimberley ter Voorde - Speelman Human Resources Assistant k.m.ter.voorde-speelman@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
