    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/coordinator-bic-assessments-orthopedagoog-2527/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Coördinator BIC-assessments/Orthopedagoog",
      "description": "Coördinator BIC-assessments/Orthopedagoog - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Coördinator BIC-assessments/Orthopedagoog Apply now Junior onderzoeker Coördinator BIC-assessments/Orthopedagoog This vacancy is only available in Dutch Het Onderzoeks- en Expertisecentrum voor Kinderen en Vreemdelingenrecht zoekt een orthopedagoog als coördinator Best interests of the Child (BIC)-assessments. Een mooie functie voor iemand die inhoudelijke expertise wil verbinden aan coördinatie, opleiding en de verdere ontwikkeling van belangen van kinderen in het migratierecht. Sinds 2005 voert het Expertisecentrum BIC-assessments uit voor kinderen die te maken hebben met een migratierechtelijke procedure. Daarbij werken we nauw samen met de beroepsverenigingen NVO en NIP: gedragswetenschappers lid van deze beroepsverenigingen voeren BIC-Assessments uit. De rapportages worden door advocaten ingebracht in de migratieprocedure. Jaarlijks worden nieuwe vrijwilligers opgeleid in de BIC-methodiek. Faculteit Gedrags- & Maatschappijwetenschappen Apply no later than: 9 november 2026 0.4 FTE €3.706 - €4.599 Share this vacancy Coördinator BIC-assessments/Orthopedagoog Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/coordinator-bic-assessments-orthopedagoog-2527/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Als coördinator coördineer je de uitvoering en versterk je de kwaliteit van de BIC-assessments. Je verzorgt mede de training van nieuwe vrijwilligers, biedt ondersteuning en supervisie aan gedragswetenschappers en studenten bij het uitvoeren van de BIC-assessments en voert zelf ook BIC-assessments uit. Daarnaast beheer en analyseer je de data die binnen de assessments worden verzameld. Een student-assistent ondersteunt je hierbij één dag per week. Een belangrijke ontwikkelopgave voor het komende jaar is de duurzame inbedding van BIC-assessments in het migratierecht. Je ondersteunt de projectleider bij het versterken van de samenwerking met ketenpartners op het gebied van kinderrechten en de positie van het belang van het kind binnen migratierechtelijke procedures. Faculteit Gedrags- & Maatschappijwetenschappen Apply no later than: 9 november 2026 €3.706 - €4.599 Wie ben jij? Je hebt aantoonbare publicaties of vergelijkbare onderzoeksoutput in peer-reviewed tijdschriften of vakpublicaties. Je hebt ervaring met het aanvragen en beheren van onderzoeksfinanciering en met budgetverantwoordelijkheid binnen projecten. Je kunt zelfstandig onderzoeksprojecten opzetten en leiden en begeleidt junior onderzoekers of promovendi effectief. Je heeft aantoonbare kennis van datamanagement, reproducible research en FAIR-principes. Je presenteert onderzoeksresultaten helder aan zowel wetenschappelijke als niet-wetenschappelijke doelgroepen en beschikt over uitstekende schrijfvaardigheid in het Nederlands en Engels. Je werkt graag interdisciplinair, draagt bij aan een inclusieve teamcultuur en bent sterk in samenwerking en stakeholdermanagement. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.706\n                                          (schaal 10)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    4.599                    (schaal 10.5)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een tijdelijk contract voor de duur van 1 jaar. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werken onderzoekers in alle takken van wetenschap en techniek aan wetenschappelijke uitdagingen en maatschappelijke vraagstukken. Docenten leiden hun studenten op voor een betekenisvolle loopbaan in de wetenschap of daarbuiten. Interdisciplinair onderzoek en onderwijs, kennis delen, participatie met bedrijven, overheidsinstellingen en maatschappelijke partijen staan bij deze top 100-universiteit hoog in het vaandel. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences (GMW) excels in research and teaching in the areas of behaviour, thinking, learning, and participation in society. More than 4,500 students and approximately 650 staff address social questions and challenges that people experience in daily life. Our core focus is on individual and societal resilience and how to strengthen it. We focus on current themes such as health and wellbeing, sustainable living, learning and development, inclusive society, safe and healthy upbringing, and work and collaboration. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences, visit rug.nl/gmw . Basiseenheid Gedrag, Opvoeding en Kinderrechten De basiseenheid Gedrag, Opvoeding en Kinderrechten (GOK) is samen met de basiseenheid Leren & Ontwikkeling verantwoordelijk voor het onderzoeks- en onderwijsprogramma Orthopedagogiek. Beide basiseenheden maken deel uit van de afdeling Pedagogische- en Onderwijswetenschappen, en werken intensief samen op het gebied van onderwijs en onderzoek. De missie van het onderzoek bij de afdeling GOK is om het ontstaan, de instandhouding en het herstel van jeugd-, gezins- en opvoedproblemen beter te begrijpen, zowel op theoretisch als op toegepast niveau. Ons onderzoek wordt gekaderd door een transactionele, ontwikkelings- en systeemgericht perspectief, waarbij we ons richten op de interactie tussen jongeren en hun omgeving (zoals het gezin, het sociale netwerk, de school en welzijnsorganisaties). Een gemeenschappelijke deler van onze onderzoeksprojecten is de focus op de complexiteit van de problemen en de klinische besluitvorming en het ingrijpen in dergelijke omstandigheden. We hebben sterke en langdurige samenwerkingen met maatschappelijke en klinische partners, nationaal en internationaal. We proberen jongeren, gezinnen en professionals zoveel mogelijk bij onze inspanningen te betrekken door een participatieve benadering te volgen. De vacature is bij de afdeling GOK en specifiek bij het Onderzoeks- en Expertisecentrum voor Kinderen en Vreemdelingenrecht. Wil je meer weten, kijk dan op Intro | Over het Onderzoeks- en Expertisecentrum | Rijksuniversiteit Groningen string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Elianne Zijlstra Universitair hoofddocent A.E.Zijlstra@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Elianne Zijlstra Universitair hoofddocent A.E.Zijlstra@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoctoral-researcher-participatory-urban-and-district-energy-planning-2563/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher participatory urban and district energy planning",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Researcher participatory urban and district energy planning - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Postdoctoral Researcher participatory urban and district energy planning Apply now Post-doc Researcher Postdoctoral Researcher participatory urban and district energy planning This vacancy is only available in English The Department of Planning and Environment of the Faculty of Spatial Sciences at the University of Groningen (RUG) is looking for a postdoctoral researcher on the topic of ‘participatory urban and district energy planning’ (0.8 fte). Faculty of Spatial Sciences Apply no later than: 31 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 0.8 FTE €3.706 - €5.760 Share this vacancy Postdoctoral Researcher participatory urban and district energy planning Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoctoral-researcher-participatory-urban-and-district-energy-planning-2563/?lang=en What are you going to do? As postdoctural researcher you will contribute to the EU Life funded CHIP-EU project. CHIP-EU aims to accelerate the decarbonisation of heating & cooling (H&C) in European cities by providing a Support Framework for developing integrated, sustainable local H&C plans. CHIP-EU prioritizes capacity building in cities to help improve the governance structures, tools, and capacity to deliver such plans, while centering on a holistic, participatory approach aligned with spatial and energy planning. CHIP-EU targets both municipalities and stakeholders, using experiential learning and training activities supported by Energy Transition Living Labs. These labs enable knowledge exchange, strengthen institutional and social capacity, and mobilise Local Energy Coalitions to enhance ownership and feasibility between public, private and civil society partners. The framework will be tested in 5 municipalities Kalamata (Greece), Valladolid (Spain), Groningen (Netherlands), Athyenou (Cyprus) and Ternopil (Ukraine), as well as the Pomurje (Slovenia). The RUG hosted postdoctoral researcher will combine general task within the full consortium, with an active contribution to the Municipality of Groningen to help them improve and upscale their previous approaches to holistic and participatory energy planning the Vinkhuizen neighborhood to a city scale. Your central tasks include: Analyzing existing H&C plans in cities on their reliance on an integrated and participatory planning approach, including a GAP Analysis on H&C Planning and Implementation. Support the development of a Guideline Book on H&C solutions that are best suited to different spatial planning concepts. Analyze local energy coalitions, energy communities and grassroots initiatives as major vehicles to achieve the local H&C transition, based on an international comparative study. Support the development of strategies and a toolkit to help develop structural forms of collaboration between various governmental and non-governmental actors, including (energy) companies, building owners, housing associations, grid companies and citizens. Conduct policy analysis, field research (i.e. a questionnaire and interviews survey), focus groups and help organize and stakeholder workshops. Contribute to project deliverables. Write academic journal to be published in open access peer reviewed journal. You will work together especially with Dr. Rozanne Spijkerboer and Prof. dr. Christian Zuidema at the Faculty of Spatial Sciences, and will also work together with colleagues from other European cities and universities in the CHIP-EU consortium. Faculty of Spatial Sciences Apply no later than: 31 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.706 - €5.760 Who are you? You are an enthusiastic and motivated researcher with: A PhD in in the wider field of spatial planning, geography, environmental policy, public administration, or another related disciplines with proven experience with spatial planning. Proven experience with the topic of energy transition, sustainable (urban) planning and participatory planning or processes. Publications in international peer-reviewed academic journals. Strong qualitative research skills with expertise in conducting in-depth interviews, policy analysis and qualitative data analysis methods. Excellent communication skills and proven experience with stakeholder engagement, including affinity with public policy processes and practices. Strong planning skills, ability to organize own work and related activities, ability to meet deadlines. Fluid English language skills (reading, writing, speaking). Dutch language skills (listening, reading, speaking) are strongly preferred. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.706\n                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    5.760                    (salary scale 10)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. 0,8 fte voor de duur van 2 jaar Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Spatial Sciences (FRW) is an interdisciplinary faculty that makes a significant impact on societal issues such as climate, broad prosperity, population decline, healthy ageing, and sustainable energy. With approximately 100 staff and over 100 PhD students, we engage daily in up-to-date and relevant teaching and research in the fields of planning, demography, and geography. Through our research programme TRACE (Transformations, Communities, and Environments), we are committed to internationally oriented, interdisciplinary research. With two Bachelor’s and seven Master’s programmes, the Faculty offers broad educational opportunities to about 1,100 students from around the world. The Faculty of Spatial Sciences plays a crucial role in understanding and shaping the living environment of the future. We work for and with society. Our motto is: we are making places better together . If you would like to learn more, visit rug.nl/frw . string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: a detailed CV including the months (not just years) when referring to your education and work experience, publications; a letter of motivation, including a description of your research interests and an explanation for why you are applying for this position (1-2 pages); the names, affiliations, and email addresses of two references who can provide letters of recommendation. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Christian Zuidema Full Professor C.Zuidema@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Christian Zuidema Full Professor C.Zuidema@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-the-roles-of-siblings-and-school-peers-in-young-adults-life-events-2530/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life events",
      "description": "Postdoc The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life events - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Postdoc The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life events Apply now Post-doc Researcher Postdoc The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life events This vacancy is only available in English The Postdoc researcher will work in the project ‘The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life-course events’, led by Principal Investigator Clara H. Mulder and funded by an Open Competition Large grant from the Dutch Science Foundation (NWO). Faculty of Spatial Sciences Apply no later than: 6 November 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 0.8 - 1 FTE €4.599 - €4.925 Share this vacancy Postdoc The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life events Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/postdoc-the-roles-of-siblings-and-school-peers-in-young-adults-life-events-2530/?lang=en What are you going to do? The Postdoc researcher will work in the project ‘The roles of siblings and school peers in young adults’ life-course events’, led by Principal Investigator Clara H. Mulder and funded by an Open Competition Large grant from the Dutch Science Foundation (NWO). The research team further includes a PhD researcher, an assistant professor who co-supervises the PhD project, and collaborators from the University of Groningen and Statistics Netherlands (CBS). In the project, we aim to identify the roles of siblings and school peers in the occurrence, timing, and outcomes of important life-course events in young adulthood. The events are leaving the parental home and returning home, residential relocations, entry into and exit from post-secondary education, and entry to the labour market. We investigate differentiation in sibling and school-peer roles with regard to advantage versus disadvantage, gender, migrant background, age, and time period. We use register data covering the entire population of young adults in the Netherlands, including family and school-peer network data, and analyse these data with advanced statistical methods. The envisaged role of the Postdoc researcher will be to work on life-course transitions with regard to education and the labour market, to collaborate with the other team members on these and other topics, and co-supervise the PhD student. The Postdoc researcher will prepare and analyse the register data, write and co-author scientific journal articles and outreach articles, and will take the lead in the organisation of stakeholder workshops. A more detailed description of the project can be found in the project proposal. In addition, the postdoctoral researcher may contribute to teaching activities at bachelor or master level within the Faculty of Spatial Sciences (to a maximum of 10% of the appointment). Faculty of Spatial Sciences Apply no later than: 6 November 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €4.599 - €4.925 Who are you? We are looking for candidates with A PhD in sociology, education science, population studies, demography, human geography, economics, or another relevant social science, completed recently (e.g. less than about a year ago) or to be completed before the starting date (around January 2027). Publications in international peer-reviewed academic journals in the field of quantitative research on themes related to the project. Excellent skills in quantitative research using register data or large survey databases. Strong conceptual thinking. Strong motivation, good communicative skills, proactive and independent work attitude. Strong planning skills, ability to organize own work and related activities, ability to meet deadlines. Proven ability to collaborate in a research team and to take the lead in organizing collaborative work. A great curiosity and enthusiasm for scientific research. Fluency in English; preferably mastering some Dutch or willing to learn Dutch. Preferably experience in supervising junior researchers, (PhD) students or assistants. Willingness to attend conferences abroad. We warmly invite you to apply for this vacancy, if you are interested and will have completed your PhD degree before the starting date (around January 2027). We ask you to write your motivation letter without the help of artificial intelligence other than for a grammar or spelling check. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    4.599\n                                          (salary scale 10.5)                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    4.925                    (salary scale 10.7)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. This full-time appointment as Postdoc researcher is temporary for 2 years. You will first be appointed for a period of 12 months. After a positive evaluation, the contract will be extended for the remaining part of the project. Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), researchers from all fields of academia and technology are working on academic challenges and societal questions. Lecturers prepare their students for meaningful careers within or outside the academic world. Interdisciplinary research and teaching, sharing of knowledge, collaboration with businesses, government institutions, and societal organizations are aspects that are of the utmost importance to this European top university. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. The Faculty of Spatial Sciences (FRW) is an interdisciplinary faculty that makes a significant impact on societal issues such as climate, broad prosperity, population decline, healthy ageing, and sustainable energy. With approximately 100 staff and over 100 PhD students, we engage daily in up-to-date and relevant teaching and research in the fields of planning, demography, and geography. Through our research programme TRACE (Transformations, Communities, and Environments), we are committed to internationally oriented, interdisciplinary research. With two Bachelor’s and seven Master’s programmes, the Faculty offers broad educational opportunities to about 1,100 students from around the world. The Faculty of Spatial Sciences plays a crucial role in understanding and shaping the living environment of the future. We work for and with society. Our motto is: we are making places better together . If you would like to learn more, visit rug.nl/frw . The Postdoc researcher will be hosted by the Population Research Centre, Faculty of Spatial Sciences (FSS), of the University of Groningen. FSS is a dynamic faculty with an open character. With approximately 120 employees and 150 PhD researchers, we focus on highly qualified education and research in the field of planning, demography and human geography. With two bachelors degrees and seven masters programmes, the faculty offers broad training opportunities to around 1,100 students all over the world. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Application procedure Step 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Step 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Step 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Step 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Step 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: CV Motivation letter Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Clara H. Mulder Full Professor C.H.Mulder@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Mirjam Berghuis Management/Office-assistant M.Berghuis@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/onderzoeker-disability-werk-en-toegankelijkheid-2504/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Researcher in Disability, Work and Accessibility",
      "description": "Onderzoeker Disability, Werk en Toegankelijkheid - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Researcher in Disability, Work and Accessibility Apply now Researcher in Disability, Work and Accessibility The University of Groningen is an internationally oriented research university with strong roots in Groningen, City of Talent. For more than four hundred years, the University has placed a high priority on the quality of research and education. We are looking for a Researcher with a teaching component to join the NWO-funded project From Workarounds to Shared Routines: The Cost of Accessibility Across Dutch Work and Income Pathways. The position is hosted by the University of Groningen and is connected to University College Groningen. University College Groningen Apply no later than: 29 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time 0.7 FTE €3.537 - €5.264 Share this vacancy Researcher in Disability, Work and Accessibility Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/onderzoeker-disability-werk-en-toegankelijkheid-2504/?lang=en What are you going to do? We are looking for a candidate who: Has completed, or will have completed before the starting date, a relevant Master’s degree in spatial sciences, human geography, planning, sociology, disability studies, public policy, health sciences, organisation studies, or social work. Demonstrates experience independently planning, conducting and analysing qualitative research. Has experience with several qualitative methods, such as interviews, focus groups, observations, shadowing, go-along methods and participatory workshops. Has experience with participatory, co-creative or stakeholder-based research in which lived experiences are central. Has relevant knowledge or experience in one or more of the following areas: disability and accessibility, inclusive environments, work participation, social inequality, public policy, health and care. Is able to connect lived experience to organisational practices, material environments and wider policy or institutional arrangements. Can work independently and take responsibility for agreed tasks while collaborating constructively within a multidisciplinary team. Can work carefully and respectfully with people with different disabilities, communication preferences and support needs, with attention to accessibility, consent, confidentiality, representation and participation burden. Is able to translate academic findings into accessible formats for professional, community, educational and public audiences. Has strong organisational and communication skills and can coordinate fieldwork, documentation, meetings and deliverables across several sites while maintaining constructive relationships with partner organisations. Has a good command of Dutch and English and is willing to travel to research and partner locations in The Netherlands. In relation to the teaching component of the job, we also expect: Affinity with teaching qualitative research methods to interdisciplinary bachelor students. The ability to explain and discuss qualitative methods clearly to students with different disciplinary backgrounds and levels of experience. Affinity with supervising student projects and supporting group collaboration. The ability to provide clear, constructive and timely feedback. Willingness to teach and assess within an existing, coordinated course and project framework. Extensive formal university teaching experience is not required. Demonstrable experience with workshops, presentations, facilitation, peer support or student supervision may also provide a relevant basis for the teaching component. University College Groningen Apply no later than: 29 October 2026 23:59 Dutch local time €3.537 - €5.264 Who are you? A PhD is not required, and recent Master’s graduates are eligible to apply. However, candidates must already have substantial relevant research experience and be ready to conduct qualitative research independently from the beginning of the appointment. The research project: From workarounds to shared routines The NWO-funded project From Workarounds to Shared Routines: The Cost of Accessibility Across Dutch Work and Income Pathways investigates how responsibility for making work accessible is distributed among disabled workers, employers, colleagues, support professionals and public institutions. The project focuses particularly on transitions into, within and out of work. It compares different Dutch employment settings and examines when accessibility depends on individual workarounds and informal support, and when it is embedded in shared and sustainable organisational routines. Through qualitative and participatory research, the project brings together the experiences of people with disabilities and chronic health conditions with the perspectives of employers, professionals and policymakers. Findings will be translated with project partners into practical tools, protocols and learning materials. Your role Within the research design and methodological framework established by the project leads, you will take day-to-day responsibility for substantial components of the empirical research. You will organise and conduct fieldwork, maintain structured and comparable case documentation, analyse qualitative material and prepare case-level and cross-case analytical contributions. You will coordinate activities with participating organisations, experts-by-experience and other project partners. The project leads retain responsibility for methodological design, comparative synthesis and overall scientific direction. Your responsibilities will include: Carrying out substantial components of multi-method qualitative research within the agreed research design, including interviews, observations, focus groups, workplace shadowing and participatory workshops. Recruiting participants and coordinating fieldwork, consent procedures, schedules and communication with participating organisations. Working collaboratively and respectfully with people with different disabilities, communication preferences and access requirements, including experts-by-experience and co-researchers. Analysing interview, observational, organisational and policy material and contributing to case studies and comparative analysis across the project settings. Maintaining secure, accurate and well-organised research data, fieldwork documentation and consent records. Organising and contributing to co-analysis sessions, stakeholder meetings, pilot activities and the development of accessible tools and research outputs. Contributing to project planning and reporting, academic and professional publications, public engagement and the coordination of clearly defined tasks undertaken by student assistants. Teaching The teaching responsibilities will primarily include: Contributing to the course Qualitative Data Collection and Analysis, including teaching, feedback and assessment. Supervising interdisciplinary bachelor-level student projects. If you recognize yourself in this role but do not yet meet all the requirements completely, do not let that hold you back from applying. We are happy to discuss your experience and explore opportunities for growth within the role together. What can you expect from us? In accordance with the collective labor agreement for Dutch universities, we offer a salary of at least €                    3.537\n                                          (salary scale 08)                    \n                    up to a maximum of €                    5.264                    (salary scale 09)\n                    gross per month for a full-time employment contract. 232 vacation hours per year, based on a 38-hour workweek (1.0 FTE). You can also work more or fewer hours in exchange for more or fewer free hours. For example, with a 40-hour workweek, you save 96 extra free hours, and with a 36-hour workweek, you lose 96 hours. End-of-year bonus of 8.3% and 8% holiday allowance. Extensive opportunities for personal and professional development. The appointment comprises 0.7 FTE for a period of four years and combines research and teaching responsibilities. UFO profile: Teaching and Research Assistant.\nIn addition:\n\nOpportunities for professional development in research, teaching and project coordination.\nAn interdisciplinary and socially engaged research and teaching environment.\nThe opportunity to contribute to a national project with direct relevance to policy, professional practice, education and the everyday lives of people with disabilities.\n\nIntended starting date: 1 December 2026 Where will you be working? At the University of Groningen (UG), you work at a broad top-class university that covers all fields of academia and technology. Support staff members offer a vital contribution to the effort made by lecturers and researchers toward the development of talent and a better, sustainable society. The UG aims to be an open academic community with an inclusive and safe working climate that invites you to add your value. University College Groningen (UCG) has offered a Liberal Arts and Sciences (LAS) programme since September 2014. With approximately 60 motivated staff members and 400 students, we are a dynamic, international, and well-connected academic community. Our programme offers a small-scale, broad, and intensive Bachelor’s degree with majors in three disciplines: humanities, social sciences, and science. Students engage in societal challenges through experiential and project-based learning, approaching complex problems from an interdisciplinary perspective. Our staff combine educational innovation with research, applying this approach to socially relevant projects that make a real impact. As a faculty, we aim to stay connected with other faculties, the region, and society and to expand our collaborations both locally and globally. If you want to know more about University College Groningen, check out rug.nl/ucg . The project is led by Prof. Bettina van Hoven at the University of Groningen. The core academic team brings together expertise in community-based participatory research, disability and inclusive cities, qualitative methodology and ethics, narrative research, inclusive employment, workplace innovation and professional education. The wider consortium includes employers, social enterprises, municipal and national public-sector organisations, care and support providers, employment intermediaries, experts-by-experience and partners in vocational and higher education. The teaching activities will be embedded in an interdisciplinary educational environment. Students come from different disciplinary backgrounds and are expected to integrate knowledge, methods and perspectives when addressing complex societal questions. string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\r\n\r\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interested? Does this vacancy appeal to you? If so, click on the button below and apply straightaway. Please add the following documents to your application: A curriculum vitae, including relevant research, coordination, public-engagement and teaching experience. A motivation letter of no more than one A4 page. Copies of relevant diplomas and transcripts. The names and contact details of two referees. Tentative interview dates: November 5th and November 6th, 2026. Apply now Do you have any questions or need more information? Questions about the content of the job? Bettina van Hoven Full Professor B.van.Hoven@rug.nl Questions about your application process? Bettina van Hoven Full Professor B.van.Hoven@rug.nl Information about applying When scheduling meetings, we will take your schedule into account as much as possible. The University of Groningen considers social safety important. We strive to be a university where staff and students feel respected and at home, regardless of differences in background, experiences, perspectives, and identity. For more information, see also our page about our diversity policy . Acquisition is not appreciated. Our selection procedure follows the guidelines of the NVP Application Code. Read document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Go straight to All vacancies Working at UG Contact information University of Groningen PO Box 72 9700 AB Groningen The Netherlands How to find us Follow us on array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/beheertechnicus-2119/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Beheertechnicus",
      "description": "Beheertechnicus - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Beheertechnicus Apply now Beheertechnicus This vacancy is only available in Dutch De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen is een van de oudste en grootste universiteiten van Nederland. Duizenden studenten en onderzoekers werken dagelijks in onze gebouwen. Dat die gebouwen en installaties gewoon werken — dat is jouw vak. Als Beheertechnicus bij de RUG ben je op operationeel niveau verantwoordelijk voor het technisch beheer en de instandhouding van een afgebakende portefeuille aan vastgoedassets en installaties. De focus ligt op controle, toezicht en kwaliteitsborging: de dingen juist doen, met behoud van beschikbaarheid, veiligheid en kwaliteit. Dit is een functie voor iemand die technische kennis combineert met een scherp oog voor kwaliteit en een stevige dosis pragmatisme. Je werkt zelfstandig, maar nooit alleen — je schakelt dagelijks met assetmanagers, gebruikers op de locaties en onderhoudspartijen. De vacature betreft een tijdelijke aanstelling van 0,8 tot 1,0 fte van 1 jaar. University Services Apply no later than: 29 oktober 2026 0.8 - 1 FTE €3.537 - €5.264 Share this vacancy Beheertechnicus Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/beheertechnicus-2119/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? •     Je loopt regelmatig rondes door gebouwen en installaties — proactief, ook samen met de onderhoudspartij. •     Je bent het aanspreekpunt voor gebruikers op locatie bij technische klachten en meldingen. •     Je controleert steekproefsgewijs of uitgevoerd onderhoud klopt — inhoudelijk en contractueel. •     Je bewaakt of storingen goed worden opgepakt: op de oorzaak, niet alleen het symptoom. •     Je stuurt bij als de kwaliteit of kosten van correctief onderhoud uit de pas lopen. •     Je werkt nauw samen met assetmanagement over de staat van installaties en terugkerende storingen. •     Je signaleert verbetermogelijkheden en koppelkansen — waar kan onderhoud slimmer worden gebundeld? University Services Apply no later than: 29 oktober 2026 €3.537 - €5.264 Wie ben jij? MBO+ werk- en denkniveau, bij voorkeur richting installatietechniek, technische bedrijfskunde of bouwkunde. Ervaring met technisch beheer van gebouwen of installaties (elektrotechnisch, werktuigbouwkundig of bouwkundig). Ervaring met gebouwbeheersystemen is een pre. Ervaring met een FMIS-systeem zoals Planon is mooi meegenomen. Je communiceert helder — naar gebruikers, leveranciers en collega’s. Je bent zelfstandig, nauwkeurig en houdt het hoofd koel als het druk is. Waarom zoek jij ons? Complexiteit die uitdaagt: de RUG beheert een omvangrijke, veelzijdige vastgoedportefeuille in het hart van Groningen. Techniek én impact: jouw werk draagt direct bij aan een veilige, duurzame en optimale omgeving voor tienduizenden studenten en medewerkers. Samenwerking op hoog niveau: je werkt nauw samen met de assetmanagers, eindgebruikers en andere afdelingen binnen de RUG. Ruimte voor ontwikkeling: uitstekende scholingsfaciliteiten en volop kansen om jouw expertise verder te verdiepen en te verbreden. Herken je jezelf in deze functie, maar voldoe je nog niet helemaal aan alle functie-eisen? Laat je daardoor niet tegenhouden om te solliciteren. We kijken graag samen naar jouw ervaring en de mogelijkheden om in de functie te groeien. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    3.537\n                                          (schaal 08)                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    5.264                    (schaal 09)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een tijdelijke aanstelling van 0,8 tot 1,0 fte van 1 jaar. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werk je bij een brede topuniversiteit, met aandacht voor alle takken van wetenschap en techniek. Ondersteunende medewerkers leveren een essentiële bijdrage aan de inzet van docenten en onderzoekers voor de ontwikkeling van talent en een betere, duurzame samenleving. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. University Services (US) is an engaged organization with over 1,250 staff members. Every day, we dedicate ourselves to creating an inspiring and sustainable academic environment in which students and staff can grow, collaborate, and reach their full potential. We support teaching, research, and operations in a progressive and collaborative way. From property maintenance to supporting the Board of the University, we proudly fulfil an important role at the University of Groningen as a facilitating and advisory service. Our services are wide-ranging and reach across the entire University. We work closely with faculties and other service units to support them as effectively as possible. If you would like to learn more about University Services, visit our website . Je komt te werken op de afdeling Vastgoedbeheer & Onderhoud, onderdeel van de Vastgoedorganisatie binnen University Services van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen. Je rapporteert aan de Teamleider Beheertechnici en werkt nauw samen met assetmanagement (AM-AO) en de afdeling Dagelijks Beheer & Monitoring. University Services ondersteunt met ruim 1.250 medewerkers het onderwijs, onderzoek en de bedrijfsvoering van de RUG — van vastgoedonderhoud en financiën tot HR, facilitaire dienstverlening en juridische zaken. string(24) \"sollicitatieprocedure_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\n\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(69) \"Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(145) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(455) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\n\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect.\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment and/or requesting references We may schedule a second interview with you. This interview can be complemented with an assessment. We may also ask for references at this point. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\n\nCurious about what the onboarding process at the University of Groningen looks like? On our information page for new employees , you can read what to expect. Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV Motivatiebrief. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Rick van der Wal Beleidsmedewerker rick.van.der.wal@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Berber Thasing HR-adviseur b.thasing@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
    },
    "https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/docent-onderwijskunde-en-pedagogiek-bij-de-universitaire-lerarenopleiding-2529/?lang=en": {
      "title": "Docent Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek bij de Universitaire Lerarenopleiding",
      "description": "Docent Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek bij de Universitaire Lerarenopleiding - Rijksuniversiteit Groningen All vacancies Working at UG Job alerts Docent Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek bij de Universitaire Lerarenopleiding Apply now Docent Docent Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek bij de Universitaire Lerarenopleiding This vacancy is only available in Dutch Wil jij bijdragen aan aan goed en kansrijk onderwijs voor alle leerlingen in Noord-Nederland? De Lerarenopleiding van de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) staat voor dit kwalitatief goed en kansrijk onderwijs. Wij willen bijdragen aan onderwijs waarin alle leerlingen zich kunnen ontwikkelen en worden voorbereid op actieve en verantwoordelijke deelname aan de samenleving. Vanuit onze verbondenheid met Noord-Nederland werken wij aan deze opdracht, samen met scholen, andere opleidingen en regionale, landelijke en internationale partners. De kernwoorden academisch, praktisch en kansrijk geven richting aan ons handelen. Academisch en praktisch komen samen in betrokken deelname aan de onderwijspraktijk en de kritische distantie daarvan. Kansrijk geeft uitdrukking aan onze verantwoordelijkheid voor de ontwikkelkansen van onze studenten en aan de opdracht om hen toe te rusten voor kansrijk onderwijs aan hun leerlingen. Wil jij hier ook aan bijdragen? In het kader van ons onderwijsprogramma, zijn we voor 0,4 fte op zoek naar een docent die in staat is de onderdelen onderwijskunde en pedagogiek, als onderdeel van de vakken die we tijdens de opleiding aan studenten aanbieden, te verzorgen op een voor aanstaande docenten geloofwaardige manier. Denk je degene te zijn die we zoeken? Solliciteer dan voor 1 november a.s. en wellicht nodigen we je dan uit voor een gesprek op 12 november a.s. Faculteit Gedrags- & Maatschappijwetenschappen Apply no later than: 31 oktober 2026 0.4 FTE €4.925 - €6.682 Share this vacancy Docent Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek bij de Universitaire Lerarenopleiding Apply now https://werkenbij.rug.nl/vacature/docent-onderwijskunde-en-pedagogiek-bij-de-universitaire-lerarenopleiding-2529/?lang=en Wat ga je doen? Je zult colleges voor onze studenten verzorgen, vooral op de woensdag (onze primaire lesdag), maar mogelijk ook op de maandag. Verder zul je actief zijn in de begeleiding en beoordeling van de studenten op de scholen en betrokken worden bij de ontwikkeling van en de uitvoering van nascholing van de Lerarenopleiding. Ervaring met het voortgezet onderwijs, opleiden en begeleiden van docenten in het VO is een vereiste. De werkzaamheden richten zich op de hieronder beschreven onderwijstaken bij de Lerarenopleiding. De onderdelen Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek worden ingezet in nauwe samenhang met de vakdidactiek en het werkplekleren op scholen. In de meeste van onze zes vakken komen beide invalshoeken aan de orde. Taken: • Ontwikkelen en verzorgen van onderwijs in Onderwijskunde en Pedagogiek op masterniveau, met name op de woensdagen. • Lesbezoeken, lesobservaties en beoordeling van het werkplekleren (de stage). • Deelname aan werkgroep voor curriculumverbetering. • Ontwikkelen en participeren in de nascholing onder de noemer van het Expertisecentrum Vakdidactiek Noord (zie de website) en in de werkgroepen van de Onderwijsregio’s voortgezet onderwijs van het Noorden. • Je bent onderdeel aan het team van de universitaire lerarenopleiding van de RUG. Faculteit Gedrags- & Maatschappijwetenschappen Apply no later than: 31 oktober 2026 €4.925 - €6.682 Wie ben jij? Voor deze functie zoeken wij iemand die beschikt over: Een afgeronde relevante universitaire master in Onderwijskunde, Pedagogiek of Ontwikkelingspsychologie. Ruime praktijkervaring als docent in het voortgezet onderwijs is een essentiële voorwaarde (bij voorkeur 5 jr of meer). Affiniteit en bij voorkeur ervaring met het opleiden en begeleiden van (aanstaande) docenten. Kennis van en ervaring in het werken met docenten en scholen. Kennis van en ervaring in toetsing en beoordeling. Gedegen kennis van wetenschappelijke ontwikkelingen op het gebied van onderwijskunde en pedagogiek. Bereidheid om over de grenzen van het eigen domein heen te kijken. Aantoonbare affiniteit met en ervaring in teamverband in internationale contexten werken. Een rijbewijs. Wat kan je van ons verwachten? Wij bieden, in overeenstemming met cao Nederlandse Universiteiten een salaris van minimaal €                    4.925\n                    \n                    tot maximaal €                    6.682                    (schaal 11)\n                    bruto per maand bij een fulltime dienstverband. 232 verlofuren per jaar, o.b.v. een 38-urige werkweek (1.0 fte). Je kunt ook meer of minder uren werken, in ruil voor meer of minder vrije uren. Zo spaar je bij een 40-urige werkweek 96 extra vrije uren en lever je bij een 36-urige werkweek 96 uur in. Eindejaarsuitkering van 8,3% en 8% vakantietoeslag. Uitgebreide mogelijkheden voor persoonlijke en professionele ontwikkeling. Een tijdelijke aanstelling van 0,4 fte voor de duur van drie jaar. Afhankelijk van het functioneren en de bedrijfsomstandigheden, kan de arbeidsovereenkomst nadien verlengd of omgezet worden in een arbeidsovereenkomst voor onbepaalde tijd. Waar ga je werken? Bij de Rijksuniversiteit Groningen (RUG) werken onderzoekers in alle takken van wetenschap en techniek aan wetenschappelijke uitdagingen en maatschappelijke vraagstukken. Docenten leiden hun studenten op voor een betekenisvolle loopbaan in de wetenschap of daarbuiten. Interdisciplinair onderzoek en onderwijs, kennis delen, participatie met bedrijven, overheidsinstellingen en maatschappelijke partijen staan bij deze top 100-universiteit hoog in het vaandel. De RUG wil een open academische gemeenschap zijn met een inclusief en veilig werkklimaat dat je uitnodigt om jouw waarde toe te voegen. The Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences (GMW) excels in research and teaching in the areas of behaviour, thinking, learning, and participation in society. More than 4,500 students and approximately 650 staff address social questions and challenges that people experience in daily life. Our core focus is on individual and societal resilience and how to strengthen it. We focus on current themes such as health and wellbeing, sustainable living, learning and development, inclusive society, safe and healthy upbringing, and work and collaboration. If you would like to learn more about the Faculty of Behavioural and Social Sciences, visit rug.nl/gmw . De Lerarenopleiding is een afdeling binnen GMW en leidt startbekwame leraren op voor het eerstegraadsbereik (master) en het tweedegraadsbereik (minor) van het voortgezet onderwijs, voert onderzoek uit en ondersteunt docenten in de regio bij hun doorlopende professionele ontwikkeling. Vanuit onze visie op kansrijk opleiden ontwikkelen we curricula en ondersteuningsinitiatieven die empirisch onderbouwd en praktijkgericht zijn, met een sterke vakdidactische en pedagogische basis. Ons onderzoeksprogramma versterkt de kwaliteit van onze opleiding en draagt nationaal en internationaal bij aan kennis over het leren van docenten in het voortgezet en hoger onderwijs. Met dit onderzoek verbeteren we interventies en implementatiestrategieën en ontwikkelen we manieren om het leren van studenten beter te organiseren en te ondersteunen. string(27) \"sollicitatieprocedure_wp_en\" array(1) {\n  [\"stappen\"]=>\n  array(5) {\n    [0]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(16) \"Your application\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n    }\n    [1]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(9) \"Selection\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n    }\n    [2]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(15) \"First interview\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n    }\n    [3]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n    }\n    [4]=>\n    array(2) {\n      [\"titel\"]=>\n      string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n      [\"uitleg\"]=>\n      string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n    }\n  }\n} array(5) {\n  [0]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(16) \"Your application\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(76) \"After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email.\"\n  }\n  [1]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(9) \"Selection\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(136) \"The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview.\"\n  }\n  [2]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(15) \"First interview\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(119) \"We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location.\"\n  }\n  [3]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(60) \"Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture   \"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(143) \"We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture.\"\n  }\n  [4]=>\n  array(2) {\n    [\"titel\"]=>\n    string(27) \"Terms of employment meeting\"\n    [\"uitleg\"]=>\n    string(167) \"After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen!\"\n  }\n} Sollicitatieprocedure Stap 1: Your application After submitting your application, you will receive a confirmation by email. Stap 2: Selection The selection committee assesses your application and you will be notified as soon as possible whether you are invited for an interview. Stap 3: First interview We would like to get to know each other better in a first interview, which can take place either online or on location. Stap 4: Second interview and possible assessment or guest lecture We may schedule a second interview with you. Depending on the position, this interview can be complemented with an assessment or guest lecture. Stap 5: Terms of employment meeting After a positive interview, we will discuss the terms of employment together. When everything is completed, we are happy to welcome you at the University of Groningen! Interesse? Klinkt dit als een uitdaging die bij je past? Solliciteer dan direct via onderstaande knop! Voeg bij je sollicitatie de volgende documenten toe: CV. Motivatiebrief. Gesprekken vinden plaats op 12 november 2026. Solliciteer nu Heb je vragen of meer informatie nodig? Heb je vragen over de inhoud van de vacature? Saskia Tuenter Docent S.Tuenter@rug.nl Heb je vragen over de sollicitatieprocedure? Wilfred van Slooten Opleidingsmanager w.f.van.slooten@rug.nl Informatie over solliciteren Bij de planning van de gesprekken houden wij zoveel mogelijk rekening met jouw agenda. De Rijksuniversiteit Groningen vindt sociale veiligheid belangrijk. We streven ernaar een universiteit te zijn waar medewerkers en studenten zich gerespecteerd en thuis voelen, ongeacht verschillen in achtergronden, ervaringen, perspectieven en identiteit. Voor meer informatie zie ook onze pagina over ons diversiteitsbeleid . Acquisitie wordt niet op prijs gesteld. Onze selectieprocedure volgt de richtlijnen van de NVP Sollicitatiecode Lees hier het document Be the first to know about vacancies at the UG Sign up for job alerts and don’t miss a single vacancy. Sign up for job alerts Jump to Alle vacatures Werken bij RUG Contactinformatie Rijksuniversiteit Groningen Postbus 72 9700 AB Groningen Waar vindt u ons Volg ons op array(11) {\n  [\"facebook\"]=>\n  string(60) \"https://www.facebook.com/universityofgroningen/?locale=nl_NL\"\n  [\"linkedin\"]=>\n  string(59) \"https://nl.linkedin.com/school/rijksuniversiteit-groningen/\"\n  [\"instagram\"]=>\n  string(48) \"https://www.instagram.com/universityofgroningen/\"\n  [\"pinterest\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"x\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"snapchat\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"tiktok\"]=>\n  string(0) \"\"\n  [\"whatsapp\"]=>\n  string(13) \"0031612345678\"\n  [\"mail\"]=>\n  string(19) \"service@gladior.com\"\n  [\"youtube\"]=>\n  string(43) \"https://www.youtube.com/universityGroningen\"\n  [\"rss\"]=>\n  string(67) \"https://www.rug.nl/about-ug/latest-news/press-information/rss-feeds\"\n} Facebook Linkedin Instagram Youtube Rss"
